 effects and followed the  ideal proportions of a Gran Turismo car  a long hood and a short rear end  in its technology the 503 was based on  the big BMW sedans the 501 and 502 the  frame engine transmission and axles were  almost identical the interior is  impressive too with its clean beauty and  1950s aesthetics three round gauges  inlaid in a metal dashboard and a few  ivory colored buttons in 1956 this was  the state-of-the-art luxury  but the 503 came at a difficult time for  BWW few people in post-war Germany could  afford such exclusive cars BMW produced  only 139 of the convertible version over  the course of five years by the late  1950s BMW was on the verge of bankruptcy  the company rescued itself with small  cars like the Zetas and the BMW 700 but  of course they didn't have the luxury or  the power of a 503 the engine the  world's first cast aluminium v8 was a  masterpiece of German engineering two  carburetors fedot fuel later versions  had outputs of 119 kilowatts at the time  even Mercedes was offering only six  cylinder engines  today a 503 convertible in good shape  will set you back a quarter of a million  euros when it comes to vintage cars  BMW's 503 is a crown jewel
 

